      "translations": {
        "en": "Then you come to the shore opposite the palm trees of the grave, perform ritual bath with dignity, and say while bathing: 'O Allah, purify me and purify my heart for me, expand my breast, and cause Your love, praise, and glorification to flow upon my tongue, for there is no power and no strength except with You. And I know that the foundation of my religion is submission to Your command and testifying concerning all Your prophets and messengers with unity among them. I testify that they are Your prophets and Your messengers to all Your creation. O Allah, make it for me a light, a purification, a protection, and a cure from every ailment and disease, and from every defect and plague, and from the evil of what I fear and guard against. O Allah, purify with it my heart, limbs, bones, flesh, blood, hair, skin, marrow, nerves, and all that the earth has taken from me, and make it a witness for me on the day of my poverty and need.'"
      }
